  "question": {
    "text": "The stopping potential <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msub></math> (in volt) as a function of frequency <math><mo>(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>)</mo></math> for a sodium emitter, is shown in the figure. The work function of sodium, form the data plotted in the figure, will be:<br />(Given: Planck&rsquo;s constant <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>6.63</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> , electron charge <math> <mrow> <mrow><mo>(</mo> <mtext>e</mtext> <mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow> </math> <math><mo>=</mo><mn>1.6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ebbd2ff1-374e-4682-aec4-feedb380c9db-image2.png\" />",
